LIBPKGRECONCILE-POSIX(3)

# NAME

libpkgreconcile-posix - persist target-bound reconciliation inventories

# SYNOPSIS

```
#include <libpkgreconcile-posix/libpkgreconcile-posix.h>

pkgreconcile::posix::inventory_generation_store store(store_path, target);

auto publication = store.publish_pending({pending});
auto resolution = store.resolve(pending);
```

# DESCRIPTION

*libpkgreconcile-posix* persists *libpkgreconcile* inventories using immutable
content-addressed generations and an atomic current selector.

Each store is durably bound to one exact
*reconciliation_target_reference*. Reopening with another target is refused.

The current implementation is Linux-hosted and uses *openat*(2), *flock*(2),
*fsync*(2), and *renameat2*(2) with no-replace semantics.

# PENDING PUBLICATION

*publish_pending()* atomically merges a batch of exact pending tuples into the
current authoritative inventory.

Absent tuples become pending. Existing pending tuples remain pending. Existing
resolved tuples remain resolved and are reported through
*suppressed_resolved()*.

Duplicate exact tuples in one request are rejected.

# RESOLUTION

*resolve()* transitions one exact existing pending tuple to resolved.

An already-resolved tuple returns *already_resolved*. An absent tuple returns
*missing* and is not invented.

# DURABILITY

Successful mutations return only after generation data and selector publication
have crossed the provider's synchronization boundary and the selected inventory
has been read back.

If a mutation throws after selector replacement, the caller may not know which
generation survived a crash. Retrying the same operation is safe because public
mutations are idempotent.

# TOMBSTONES

Resolved records remain in authoritative generations and suppress exact replay.
Version 0.1.0 provides no automatic tombstone retirement.

# BOUNDARIES

The library does not discover rejected evidence, interpret rejected-object
locators, reopen retained objects, infer package ownership, mutate target package
paths, publish installed state, present merge policy, or orchestrate package
transactions.

# FILES

_/usr/include/libpkgreconcile-posix/_
	Installed C++ headers.

_/usr/lib/pkgconfig/libpkgreconcile-posix.pc_
	pkg-config metadata.

# ERRORS

Store path, locking, target-binding, corruption, and durability failures are
reported as *pkgreconcile::posix::store_error*.

Cross-target mutations and duplicate publication request tuples are reported as
*std::invalid_argument*.

# SEE ALSO

*libpkgreconcile*(3)
